1.CASE OVERVIEW:
 INCIDENT TYPE: suspicious login activity 
 CATEGORY: authentication security 
 ROLE: junior SOC analyst
SEVERITY: undetermined - further inestigation required 
STATUS: under investigation 
ENVIRONMENT : simulated security operations center (SOC)

2.OBJECTIVE :
 the objective of this investigation is to analyze authentication logs, identify unusual login 
patterns, assess potential account compromise ,and recommend appropiate follow-up actions based 
on the available evidence .

3. SCENARIO DESCRIPTION :
 Northstar Solution is a fictional organization. Its security monitoring system recorded multiple authentication 
events associated with the user account Maria.s 
The events included succesful logins from two different IP addresses , a failed authentication attempt 
and a subsequent successful login. 
The purpose of this investigation is to determine whether the activity may indicate unauthorized access

